{"mathematical_payload":{"statement":"For all integers a and b, if a and b are even then a+b is even.","steps":["Let a and b be integers and assume Even(a) and Even(b).","By definition of even (claim.even_definition.v1), there exist k,m in Z with a = 2k and b = 2m.","Compute a + b = 2k + 2m = 2(k + m).","Since k and m are integers, k + m is an integer. Therefore a + b = 2(k + m) is twice an integer, so Even(a + b) by the definition of even."],"witness":"k + m"},"referenced_entity_ids":["claim.even_definition.v1"],"result_type":"proof_attempt","schema_version":"2.0.0","target_claim_id":"claim.even_sum.v1"}